(Stage 1e2 - cycle/depth safety. Inserting a map into itself makes a
 cycle; printing it recurses to the shared 64-deep _print_depth budget,
 prints a "..." truncation marker, sets the error flag, and unwinds
 safely (no stack overflow). The `on error` handler observes the flag.
 Acceptance: 64 nested levels, then ..., then truncated.)

a map called "m" is {"a": 1}.
set m's "self" to m.
print m.
on error print "truncated".